# No push until the user says so

- **Never** `git push origin main` (or any push to `main`) unless the user clearly asks in that message — e.g. “push to main”, “push all to main”, “merge to main”.
- **Never** Netlify-deploy / production publish unless they explicitly ask to deploy.
- Local `git commit` is fine when the session’s commit rules allow it; pushing is separate and always gated.
- If unsure whether they asked to push, **do not push** — ask first.
- This overrides any habit of auto-pushing after a hotfix or “so they can test on the phone.”
